fact WorkItem(id: "WI-145", description: some(value: "Proposal 032 — citation by label, not head functor. Under proposal 032 the head IS the rule's conclusion (e.g. 'gte(?x, 3.0)'); head functors are no longer unique rule identifiers, since many rules can share the same head functor (every positive arithmetic theorem has 'gte'/'lte' etc. as its head). The rule's identity for cite-resolution must therefore be the LABEL, not the head functor. Today's transitional load (rustland) papers over this by synthesizing a 0-arg label-functor as the KB head, but that's not the right architecture long-term: it forces an artificial KB term and prevents downstream code from using the head as the actual semantic claim. Migration: (a) cite-resolution (anthill-cli/src/prove.rs and any 'using' lookup paths) consults a label→rule map keyed on the rule's label, falling back to head functor only for unlabeled legacy rules; (b) by_functor index for SLD continues to use head functor (multi-rule per functor is fine for SLD); (c) loader stops synthesizing the label-functor head — labeled rules use the user's head term as the KB head directly. Depends on WI-143 (smt-gen migration). Acceptance: cargo test green; multi-head labeled rules work end-to-end; lf1 reachability_band cites work without the synthesized-functor workaround."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-143"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-16T19:22:26Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-145", author: "user", content: "Loader desugars labeled multi-head rules into N labeled rules sharing the label (kb/load.rs load_rule); 0-arg label-functor head synthesis dropped from loader and from synthesize_step_rule (prove.rs). New KB API rule_ids_by_qn returns all rids for a qn (label-first, by_functor fallback). lift_rule_to_implication_clause now returns Vec<String> and fans out one clause per rid via lift_one_rid; render_cited_lemmas extends the cite list with the lifted vec. smt-gen HeadShape::LabelFunctor arm dropped (along with its rule_conclusion read); classify_head's 0-arg branch now falls to Bottom for both denial and 0-arg predicate heads (preserves existing behavior). assert_rule_debruijn_in_frame drops its conclusion parameter (only caller was synthesize_step_rule, which now uses head_term directly). The legacy assert_rule_debruijn_with_conclusion + rule_conclusion + RuleEntry.conclusion field are now provably dead — left in place for WI-144 to delete. Tests: full workspace cargo test --no-fail-fast green (45/45 binaries, 0 failures); anthill-smt-gen integration suite 23/23 (new lift_fans_out_one_clause_per_labeled_head replaces the old multi-and assertion); lf1 discharge.sh: 14 proved / 0 failed (reachability_band — the lf1 labeled multi-head case called out in WI-145 acceptance — discharges as before). simplify pass: restored rule_id_by_qn to a direct label/by_functor lookup (the initial rewrite of it as a .into_iter().next() over rule_ids_by_qn allocated a Vec on every call, regressing the SMT lift hot path); trimmed change-narration prose from the lift doc-comment. Out of scope: dropping the dead conclusion field + accessor + with-conclusion helper (WI-144, which now lists WI-145 as a hard dependency).", at: "2026-05-16T19:22:26Z")
